Starting with kernel 2.6.13, my system crashes immediately reading from
one of my two Nakamichi MJ-5.16S SCSI CD changers. For info on this
device, see http://www.nakamichi.co.jp/download/MJ516S_J.PDF

Sorry, this pdf is in japanese only. It's a CD changer that takes 5 CD's
and loads the cd by opening the device that corresponds to the LUN.
It has 1 SCSI ID and 5 LUNs.

It happens always and immediately when I mount a data CD, or when I rip 
an audio CD.
Oops data has to be captured from a serial console.

Until Kernel 2.6.12, everything was fine. Problem still is there in 
2.6.15-rc6.

I'm using Fedora Core 4 x86_64 on a dual core Athlon 64 x2 4400+

Thanks for any help, following are the details.

Pim


